      "reading": "the uniform history barycentre is the best query point: leaning on the recency (2^-i weights) or on the last item alone loses a fifth of the correlation, so the metric wants the whole sequence, not its tail"
    },
    "round_9_finding": "The generator-side view is negatively correlated (-0.3669): a level-1 cell that answers the query by itself leaves Stage 3's re-ranking nothing to choose from, and the top ten fills with near-duplicates. Its complement -- the room the re-ranking has inside the cell -- is positively correlated (+0.3669). Together with the path likelihood (-0.2823) this says the same thing twice: a good SID is a COARSE prefix with diverse candidates, not a tight one that answers on its own.",
    "teacher_sweep": {
      "pairwise_reference_history_barycentre": 0.7623,
      "pairwise_reference_single_anchor": 0.6592,
      "pairwise_reference_recency_weighted": 0.4533,
      "next_item_reference_prediction": 0.3052,
      "reading": "the pairwise teacher's source tower carries more of the user's direction than a next-item predictor trained on the mean-pooled history: the intent model loses the order and the recency of the sequence and with them the signal the metric reads"
    },
    "round_10": "Two constructions new in construction were measured and neither is eligible: the cross-fitted FULL-NEGATIVE expected rank over all 256 cells scores -0.0787, where the LOCAL contrast over ten negatives scores +0.5824, and the cell-REMOVAL construction scores +0.1225. The signal is local: the table has to contrast the true item against a few negatives, and a global ranking or a removal is a property of the reference's geometry instead.",
    "new_families": {
      "gromov_prefix_alignment": {
        "all_107": 0.499,
        "fresh_77": 0.4375,
        "note": "a FOURTH family that works, and a different construction from the local contrast: it asks whether the hyperbolic shared depth of a pair and the length of their shared SID prefix agree, over the training pairs"
      },
      "tree_distortion": "the mirror of the alignment; its negation is the eligible form",
      "cone_consistency": 0.0866
    }
  },
